Z||000000||JohnnyK||04-19-2000||04:57 PM||||To all those who have done this, how do I remove the long screw/shaft that goes through the clutch and brake pedal.. (I'm trying to put on the new steel pedal).. I took off the 15mm bolt on the end, and I know you are supposed to pull it through so it is through the clutch pedal (to remove the pedal), but not the brake pedal, but I can't get that long screw to slide through? I thought it would just slide through once that bolt is removes, but it doesn't.. And theres no way I have to screw it through, because that would be impossible?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-19-2000||07:51 PM||||JohnnyK, I just did mine and you are right,  it should just slide through. Will the bolt turn at all? Try to wiggle the bolt at the same time press the brake pedal. I think it may just be binding up.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||04-19-2000||08:05 PM||||I think he's right that it's binding on those crappy plastic washers. If the washers arent nice and smooth you can get new ones at those emergency repair part displays that have door handles, springs, clips etc.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-20-2000||10:51 AM||||all bushings & washers are at Home Depot||||reg||14
